CaseRecord Specification {#chapter-caserecord}
=======================================

## Definition ## {#section-caserecord-definition}

A <dfn>CaseRecord</dfn> is a [=Record=] whose Record type is the Root CaseRecord Schema or a subclass of it (see [[#section-schemarecord-basedon]]). It links Records that belong together. A CaseRecord MUST NOT be a container and MUST NOT contain the content of the Records to which it relates. A Record linked by a CaseRecord remains an independent Record.

The content of a Version of a CaseRecord is a JSON object in the primary representation (format `application/json`). It is defined by the Root CaseRecord Schema:

<table class="data">
<thead><tr><th>Field<th>Required<th>Type<th>Description</thead>
<tr><td><code>title</code><td>MAY<td>String<td>Human-readable title of the Case in this Version
<tr><td><code>trigger</code><td>MAY<td>Array&lt;DID&gt;<td>Records that triggered the Case
<tr><td><code>context</code><td>MAY<td>Array&lt;DID&gt;<td>Records relevant to understanding and processing the Case
<tr><td><code>process</code><td>MAY<td>Array&lt;DID&gt;<td>Records documenting the processing steps
<tr><td><code>decision</code><td>MAY<td>Array&lt;DID&gt;<td>Records documenting the decision
<tr><td><code>result</code><td>MAY<td>Array&lt;DID&gt;<td>Records documenting the outcome
</table>

No field is required. A schema based on the Root CaseRecord Schema MAY require fields and MAY add fields. It MUST NOT remove or change the meaning of the fields defined here. A field that is present MAY be an empty array. A Record MAY appear in more than one field.

RWP assigns no semantics to the field names beyond the descriptions above. The relationship of a linked Record to the Case in more specific terms (for example "legal basis") is expressed by an [=AssertionRecord=], not by the CaseRecord.

<pre class="example json" title="CaseRecord content">
{
  "title": "Building permit Musterstrasse 12, parcel 451",
  "trigger":  [ "did:rwp:&lt;namespace&gt;:&lt;recordId&gt;:&lt;versionHash&gt;" ],
  "context":  [ "did:rwp:&lt;namespace&gt;:&lt;recordId&gt;:&lt;versionHash&gt;" ],
  "process":  [ "did:rwp:&lt;namespace&gt;:&lt;recordId&gt;" ],
  "decision": [],
  "result":   []
}
</pre>


## Taxonomy ## {#section-caserecord-taxonomy}

<pre class="highlight language-text">
@prefix rw: &lt;https://w3id.org/recordweb/ontology#&gt; .
rw:CaseRecord
  rdfs:subClassOf rw:RelationRecord .
</pre>

## Links ## {#section-caserecord-links}

Every entry of trigger, context, process, decision and result is a <dfn>Link</dfn>: the DID of a Record ([[#chapter-identity]]). A Link is a Hard Link or a Soft Link as defined in [[#section-identity-hash]]. A Link MAY identify any Record, including another CaseRecord. A Link from CaseRecord A to CaseRecord B refers only to B (or the identified Version of B). It MUST NOT be treated as a link from A to the Records linked by B. A Record is a direct member of CaseRecord A only if A links to it explicitly.


## Finalisation ## {#section-caserecord-finalisation}

Before a Version of a CaseRecord is finalised, the producer MUST verify that every Link in its content is a Hard Link, and that every Hard Link can be resolved to a finalised Version of the identified Record, subject to the applicable federation and offline-validation rules.

If a check fails, the producer MUST NOT finalise the Version and MUST return the Links that failed. A notification, callback or other message received through Source Integration MAY trigger a refresh or retry. It MUST NOT replace this verification.

A Version without any Link MAY be finalised. A schema based on the Root CaseRecord Schema MAY impose further requirements. It MUST NOT relax the requirements of this section.